-- title:
--   Source-full mixed goodness bounds the localized defect
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be finite with decidable equality, $P$ an ordered coarse-fine complex, $A$ a closed atom configuration in its coarse complex, and $e$ a positive ordered face. If $A$ is source-full mixed-good at $e$ for real parameters $\alpha,\beta$, then its localized mixed defect square is at most $\beta$ times the mean of its mixed boundary weight.
